	  <td valign="top">  

  <FONT size="+1"><B>UNBRIDLED AGGRESSION REGULATIONS AND CODE OF CONDUCT</B></FONT>
	<p><B>Scribed 14 January 2001</B>
<table>
<tr><td><p><B>Invitations:</B></td></tr>
<tr><td>Any player wanting to join UA must first satisfactorily complete a probation period of not more than two weeks (rl time). During this time, the applicant must group with at least one other UA member or group of members three times. The applicant will not be allowed to wear the UA tag until the probationary period has been completed and a vote has been taken by the council, class captain and other ranking officers, thus meaning the individual would remain on anon, but still be allowed to take part in guild chat, activities, etc. I the grouping requirements are met prior to the two-week time span, early induction can be considered. The only exceptions to this policy will be if the applicant is an alternate of an existing UA member, which must be clarified and posted by the original member. Another exception will be if the applicant has previously grouped with an established member or members an equal amount of times as stated above. These persons or person must still be voted on by the council, class captain and ranking officers. Longtime friends or hunting partners of established UA members are definite candidates for this type of consideration, however the member presenting them for consideration will be known as their "sponsor". This will also be the case for unknown applicants. Whoever would invite them would be known as sponsor for that particular individual. All applicants must be introduced "in game" or via message board to the corresponding class captain. Upon induction, it will be the class captains responsibility to post the new members level and race so that our board can be kept up to date effectively. Anyone being proposed must also be posted on the page by his or her sponsor to make everyone aware that the person is a candidate. The two-week period will begin upon proposal of induction to guild. Anyone not completing the necessary requirements will no longer be considered, but may start the probation period over if desired. The only exceptions here will be for extreme circumstances, but will still require a vote of the council, class captain and ranking officers. It will be the sponsors duty to make new prospective members aware of all requirements of becoming a member of UA. Applicants may withdraw their candidacy at any time, but future consideration will require a vote of the council, class captain and ranking officers and completion of probationary period again.</td></tr>
<tr><td><B>Primary Characters and Alternates:</B></td></tr>
<tr><td>Primary characters will be defined as those characters that are played most often and usually are of higher level than someone's lower level characters. Every member must establish and let it be known which character is their primary. Primary characters will be granted every benefit afforded regular members. They will also be the only characters allowed to participate in guild events, raids, etc. No alternates will be assisted in any way unless the member assisting is doing so of his own free will. Alternates will not be expected to ask for any guild assistance under any circumstances. Alternate characters will be posted on member directory with primaries name included with it. The alternate is solely the responsibility of the primary. If any member offers to help an alternate, you must make them aware of the fact that the character being played is an alternate. There will also only be one primary for each individual. It's your choice who to designate as that character, so do so carefully, as you will not be able to change it once it is established unless you bring it before the council and have a legitimate reason for wanting to do so. At that time the proper measures will be discussed. There will be no exceptions to this, barring that the council and ranking officers deem that you do, in fact, have a legitimate argument. Anyone removing their primary from UA will not be required to also remove their alternates, but the primaries rank, guild position, etc. Will not be transferred to the alternate. The alternate will remain listed as an alternate and all above statements will still apply. Anyone removing their character from UA and wishing to be reinstated will require a vote of the high council, class captain and ranking officers. Seniority will not be carried over. Thus a class captain leaving will not be allowed to reenter as the respective class captain.</td></tr>
<tr><td><B>Grouping and Looting:</B></td></tr>
<tr><td>It is not required to group with guildmates, although it is highly encouraged and tends to be much more fun. It also displays a sense of unity to the Norrathian world. Whether grouped or not, all UA members will be expected to conduct themselves with maturity and professionalism. Kill stealing, which is defined as killing something that someone is already engaged with will not be tolerated at all. Accidents sometimes happen, but repetitive reports of ks'ing will be brought before the council for review. Another problem within EQ is ninja looting, which is looting one kill while the group is engaged with another mob. This also will not be tolerated and it is practically impossible to loot a no drop item accidentally. These two items have been long-standing rules of UA and will be dealt with severely by the council, class captain and ranking officers. To sum it up, there will be zero tolerance in these situations.</td></tr>
<tr><td><B>Guild Chat:</B></td></tr> 
<tr><td>The guild chat channel is a very useful tool for our guild. Many members have expressed concern over certain subjects and vulgarities. Members of UA will be expected to refrain from using vulgarity over guild chat. Lewd subjects will also not be discussed. There is a filter known as /tell if anyone feels it necessary to use such innuendos. At the same time, it still may not be appreciated so please watch what you are saying. Anyone seen using profanity and/or unnecessary language will promptly receive a tell from an officer or their captain. Certain words are acceptable, but most are not. Anyone receiving a tell from an officer will be expected to abide by what will be considered a polite "hey don't do that". Any rude or disrespectful retort will result in the incident being reported to the council or class captain and the proper measures will be taken. Joking around is perfectly acceptable as long as it remains within the boundaries of good taste. This is called respecting your fellow guild members.</td></tr>
<tr><td><B>General Conduct:</B></td></tr> 
<tr><td>UA members are among the most respectful and considerate people on EQ. It will be required that you treat everyone with the same respect that you would expect. That includes everyone on our server, not just UA members. Name-calling, arguing, rudeness or inappropriate actions are not expected from UA members. If there is a problem or disagreement, please get a mediator if necessary, especially where fellow members are involved. We do not need dissention among the ranks, as it tends to tear down any productivity. Actually, it is considered rather childish and UA did not get where it is today by being any less than the best. If anyone arrives at a problem with anyone within UA, please talk with your captain, a council member or a ranking officer about it. The problem will almost surely dissipate.</td></tr>
<tr><td><B>Guild Meetings:</B></td></tr> 
<tr><td>It has been agreed that the ranking officers, high council and class captains will hold a meeting every first Saturday of each month. These meetings will be held at the arena in lake rathe. This will keep everyone abreast of the happenings within the guild. All those that are a part of this group are expected to attend. Those that aren't will politely be asked to excuse themselves, unless their presence has also been requested. We are aware that there will be times when someone can't possibly make it. Once again, the day of these meetings has been established, so any excuses barring extenuating circumstances will not be acceptable. You all were asked if you wanted these positions and you all agreed to them. Responsibilities to the guild came with it. Class captains that absolutely cannot make meetings would be asked to have their lt. stand in for them so that they can let the captain know what happened. Those not having a lt. are encouraged to ask and appoint one. These lt's need not be officers, as I believe we have enough officers as it is. When it comes time to appoint more, the topic will be discussed. Airez will oversee the meetings, as he is the c.e.o. of the high council.</td></tr>
<tr><td><B>Guild Tag:</B></td></tr> 
<tr><td>From here on, if you are an established member of UA, you will not be expected to be anon for any reason. We are very proud of our guild and frankly, there is no excuse to be anon. if you are receiving tells, etc. Wanting you to perform some task such as teleporting, heals, binds etc. /roleplay has the same effect as anon, but keeps the guild tag intact. The only people that should be completely anon are those new people currently under consideration for membership. Anyone seen without the tag will be asked to switch to /roleplay. Anyone seen that is being considered that is not anon will be required to go to anon immediately.</td></tr>
<tr><td><B>Basic Summary of UA Regulations and Code of Conduct</B></td></tr> 
<tr><td>UA has been growing very rapidly and with that came many different perspectives and opinions. We felt it necessary to implement a few do's and don'ts so that everyone would know exactly what we were all about and what was expected of them as a member of UA. We don't expect these regs and such to detract from the fun or enjoyment of the game. We merely wanted everyone to be aware that as a member of UA, you represent the entire guild. If you wrong someone, they will remember the guild name long after they have forgotten yours. Hold your heads high and don't be intimidated by anyone or any guild. We are no better than anyone else, but they are certainly no better than UA. I'm sure everyone can live with this, as it will make us a better and closer family than we already are... which is what a great guild is all about in the first place.</td></tr>
</table>	
  <p align="right"><I> - By decree of the Unbridled Aggression High Council.</p>

	

      </td>
	</tr>
